  4. Population Counts by age and sex (ADM-0)
  Below, we compare the population structure across sex and age groups between the NSO and WPP
  projections at the national level. The sex and age specific population counts of this COD-PS at ADM-0
  are generally consistent with the WPP ADM-0 projection, though this COD-PS projects somewhat lower
  numbers of youths aged 5-19 than the WPP. For the 5-9 age group, for example, this COD-PS projects
  8.33% fewer males and 6.53% fewer females than the WPP. These differences in the projected
  population of children could be shaped by assumptions around fertility since the 2005 census.
